	it proves the crosswise EPR exchange independently, without assuming
	symmetry of the strategy. The permutation of the six registers
	exchanging $\mathsf{A}' \leftrightarrow \mathsf{B}''$ and
	$\mathsf{A}'' \leftrightarrow \mathsf{B}'$ fixes $\ket{\hat\psi}$, since
	each EPR vector is symmetric, and carries the placement
	$\mathsf{A}\mathsf{A}'$ to $\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}''$ and
	$\mathsf{B}\mathsf{A}''$ to $\mathsf{B}\mathsf{B}'$. Consequently, for
	every operator $P$ on $\hilb \ot (\C^q)^{\ot M}$,
	$\lVert (P)_{\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}''} \ket{\hat\psi} \rVert
	= \lVert (P)_{\mathsf{A}\mathsf{A}'} \ket{\hat\psi} \rVert$ and
	$\lVert (P)_{\mathsf{B}\mathsf{B}'} \ket{\hat\psi} \rVert
	= \lVert (P)_{\mathsf{B}\mathsf{A}''} \ket{\hat\psi} \rVert$. Each
